  "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $Y$ is a function $F(y)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(y)=P(Y\\le y).\n$$\n\nComputing $F(1)$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1) & =P(Y\\le 1) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {0,1}) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1) \\\\  & =0.343+0.441 \\\\  & =0.784.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $F(2)$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(2) & =P(Y\\le 2) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {0,1,2}) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1)+f(2) \\\\  & =0.343+0.441+0.189 \\\\  & =0.973.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nF(2)-F(1)=0.973-0.784=0.189\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
